            "summary": "",
            "theoryHtml": "\n            <h3>National Mineral Exploration Trust (NMET): Unlocking Subterranean Wealth</h3>\n            <p>India’s geological landmass is extraordinarily prospective, sharing identical Gondwanaland Precambrian metallogenic provinces with mineral-rich Western Australia, Southern Africa, and South America. However, historically, <strong>over 95% of Indian mineral production was confined to shallow surface and near-surface deposits (depths less than 50–100 meters)</strong>, while deep-seated, concealed, and blind ore bodies remained unexplored due to lack of high-risk exploration venture capital. To overcome this critical bottleneck, the MMDR Amendment Act, 2015 created the <strong>National Mineral Exploration Trust (NMET)</strong> under <strong>Section 9C</strong> of the Act.</p>\n\n            <h4>1. Institutional Mandate & Governance Architecture</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>Statutory Body:</strong> Established by the Central Government under Section 9C of the MMDR Act as an autonomous statutory non-profit trust.</li>\n                <li><strong>Funding Architecture:</strong>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li>Funded by a statutory levy on mining leaseholders equivalent to <strong>2% of the statutory royalty paid</strong> on all major minerals.</li>\n                        <li>Has accumulated an exploration corpus exceeding <strong>₹4,000 to ₹5,000 crore</strong>, providing dedicated funding for high-risk, capital-intensive exploration projects without relying on budgetary allocations.</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </li>\n                <li><strong>Governing Structure:</strong> Chaired by the <strong>Union Minister of Mines</strong> (Governing Body), with an Executive Committee headed by the <strong>Secretary, Ministry of Mines</strong>.</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>2. Key Exploration Priorities Funded by NMET</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>1. Deep-Seated & Concealed Mineral Deposits:</strong> Funding 3D seismic profiling, deep stratigraphic diamond-core drilling, and multi-sensor hyperspectral airborne geophysics for copper, lead, zinc, gold, silver, and diamond kimberlites.</li>\n                <li><strong>2. Critical, Strategic & Rare Earth Minerals:</strong> Specialized exploration for Lithium, Cobalt, Nickel, Gallium, Germanium, Niobium, Tantalum, and REEs to build domestic energy transition supply chains.</li>\n                <li><strong>3. Accreditation of Private Exploration Agencies:</strong> Under recent reforms, NMET has accredited dozens of private sector exploration companies to conduct baseline exploration projects with 100% financial reimbursement from NMET!</li>\n            </ul>\n        ",
