            "summary": "",
            "theoryHtml": "\n            <h3>The Indian Lithium Miracle: Salal-Haimana (J&K) & Katghora (Chhattisgarh)</h3>\n            <p><strong>Lithium ($Li$)</strong> is the lightest metallic element in the periodic table ($Z = 3$, atomic weight 6.94). Possessing the highest electrochemical potential (-3.04 V) and an extraordinarily high energy density, lithium forms the indispensable chemical core of <strong>Lithium-Ion Batteries (LIBs)</strong> powering electric vehicles, smartphones, grid-scale renewable energy storage, and satellite communications.</p>\n\n            <h4>1. Salal-Haimana Discovery (Reasi District, Jammu & Kashmir)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>The Historic Announcement:</strong> In February 2023, the Geological Survey of India (GSI) announced the landmark discovery of an estimated <strong>5.9 million tonnes of Inferred Lithium Resources (G3 level)</strong> in the <strong>Salal-Haimana area of Reasi district, Jammu & Kashmir</strong>.</li>\n                <li><strong>Global Significance:</strong> If confirmed through detailed G2/G1 drilling, this resource would position India among the top 7 nations globally in lithium reserves, trailing only Bolivia, Argentina, the US, Chile, Australia, and China!</li>\n                <li><strong>Geological Occurrence:</strong>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li>Unlike the salar brines of South America or granitic pegmatites (spodumene) of Australia, the Salal-Haimana deposit is a <strong>clay/bauxite-associated lithium deposit</strong>.</li>\n                        <li>Lithium is concentrated within a bauxitic-aluminous laterite crust resting unconformably upon the Proterozoic Sirban Limestone.</li>\n                        <li>Assays show average lithium concentrations ranging from <strong>500 to 1,000+ parts per million (ppm)</strong> (with local values up to 1,500 ppm).</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>2. Katghora (Korba District, Chhattisgarh): India’s First Auctioned Lithium Block</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li>In 2024, the Ministry of Mines successfully completed the competitive commercial e-auction of the <strong>Katghora Lithium and Rare Earth block in Korba district, Chhattisgarh</strong>.</li>\n                <li>Won by a private mining entity (Maheswari Mining), Katghora marked India's historic maiden commercial award of a domestic lithium exploration and mining concession!</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>3. Global Lithium Context: The 'Lithium Triangle' vs Hard Rock</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>The Lithium Triangle (South America):</strong> <strong>Chile, Bolivia, and Argentina</strong> hold over 50% of the world’s lithium, hosted within high-altitude continental salt flat brines (salars like Atacama and Uyuni), extracted via solar evaporation ponds.</li>\n                <li><strong>Hard Rock Pegmatites (Australia):</strong> Western Australia (Greenbushes, Pilgangoora) is the world's largest exporter of lithium, mining hard-rock lithium aluminum silicate called <strong>Spodumene ($LiAlSi_2O_6$)</strong>.</li>\n            </ul>\n        ",
