            "summary": "",
            "theoryHtml": "\n            <h3>Khanij Bidesh India Limited (KABIL): India's Global Mineral Envoy</h3>\n            <p>To overcome India’s complete domestic deficit in critical energy transition minerals like Lithium, Cobalt, and Nickel, the Government of India realized that relying solely on open-market spot imports exposed the economy to catastrophic geopolitical embargoes. In August 2019, the Ministry of Mines incorporated a dedicated overseas investment vehicle: <strong>Khanij Bidesh India Limited (KABIL)</strong>.</p>\n\n            <h4>1. Corporate Architecture & Equity Structure of KABIL</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>Public Sector Joint Venture:</strong> KABIL was established through a strategic equity partnership among three premier central public sector enterprises (CPSEs) under the Ministry of Mines:\n                    <ol>\n                        <li><strong>National Aluminium Company Limited (NALCO):</strong> <strong>40% equity share</strong></li>\n                        <li><strong>Hindustan Copper Limited (HCL):</strong> <strong>30% equity share</strong></li>\n                        <li><strong>Mineral Exploration and Consultancy Limited (MECL):</strong> <strong>30% equity share</strong></li>\n                    </ol>\n                </li>\n                <li><strong>Strategic Mandate:</strong> To identify, explore, acquire, develop, mine, and process strategic and critical mineral assets abroad for commercial supply to the Indian domestic market.</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>2. Historic Breakthrough: The Argentina Lithium Acquisition (January 2024)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>First-Ever Overseas Lithium Agreement:</strong> On January 15, 2024, KABIL signed a historic agreement with <em>CAMYEN SE (Catamarca Minera y Energética Sociedad del Estado)</em>, a state-owned mining enterprise of the Catamarca province in Argentina.</li>\n                <li><strong>The Concession:</strong>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li>Acquired exploration and commercial exploitation rights for <strong>5 lithium brine blocks</strong> (Cortadera-I, Cortadera-VII, Cortadera-VIII, Cateo-2022-018, and Cortadera-VI) covering an area of approximately <strong>15,703 hectares</strong> in the Fiambalá area of Catamarca province.</li>\n                        <li>KABIL committed an investment of <strong>₹200 crore (~$24 million)</strong> over five years for exploration, brine extraction, and pilot plant establishment.</li>\n                        <li><strong>Significance:</strong> Represents the <strong>first-ever overseas exploration and mining project undertaken by an Indian government enterprise for lithium</strong>, directly planting the Indian flag within the global 'Lithium Triangle'!</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>3. Critical Mineral Partnerships with Australia</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li>KABIL executed a Government-to-Government (G2G) agreement with the <strong>Critical Minerals Facilitation Office (CMFO) of Australia</strong>.</li>\n                <li>Engaged in joint due diligence on multiple lithium and cobalt exploration projects in Western Australia, securing long-term offtake rights for Indian battery gigafactories.</li>\n            </ul>\n        ",
